      "text": "One thing about us Yemenis, we absolutely love to cook the hell out of the food especially the meat very very slowly to keep its juices, most standard meals are cooked and served extremely hot in those stone/rock pots called \"haradha\" which really intensity the taste and give a unique aroma. \nBlended fenugreek foam is also very popular, it's salty, sour and bitter with blended garlic, leek, parsley, green chili and mint, once you develop a taste for it on top of the meat stew dishes, you'll understand why it's standard in Yemeni cuisine. Fenugreek is extremely healthy, but if it's your first time you'll feel like you've had some laxative. 😁",
